<%#
  008 FR-003: the horizontal lockup — mark beside wordmark — used in the site
  header on every page.

  The wordmark is live HTML text, not SVG paths. That keeps it selectable and
  natively announced, gives FR-027's fallback for free (if the SVG fails to
  render there is still a styled, correctly coloured, clickable wordmark), and
  keeps `click_on "LockSwap"` working: Capybara matches links by visible text,
  and this project does not set Capybara.enable_aria_label, so an image-only
  brand would break test/system/navigation_test.rb.

  The two spans carry no whitespace between them so the accessible name reads
  as the single word "LockSwap".
%>
<%= link_to root_path, class: "brand-lockup" do %>
  <%# 011 FR-003: the mark pulses here too, on every page. Not the wordmark
      beside it — the loop is on the artwork, and a wordmark dimming in step
      with it would read as the lock-up coming apart rather than breathing. %>
  <%= render "shared/brand_mark", size: 32, pulse: true %>
  <span class="brand-wordmark"><span class="brand-wordmark-lock">Lock</span><span class="brand-wordmark-swap">Swap</span></span>
<% end %>
